  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The forecast remains on track into the\nweekend as storm activity winds down over the region. The trough \nexit on Saturday will result in a much more stable atmosphere, \nbut weak storm potential does persist in far eastern Nevada. \n\nSunday through Tuesday are expected to be dry, with a slow warming\ntrend due to developing ridging over the West. This will result \nin high temperatures just below normal for this time of year, with\nhighs in the upper 80s. While model agreement has increased \nsignificantly for the first half of the week, the forecast for \nlate week remains variable, with disagreement focusing on the \ntiming of a West Coast trough impact. The slower solution would \nmaintain warm and dry conditions through next weekend while the \nfaster solution would bring cooler temperatures and storm \npotential as early as Thursday or Friday.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in weakening\nstorms by Saturday. Moderate confidence in dry weather and near \nnormal temperatures through Wednesday. Low confidence past \nWednesday. No changes from the NBM.",
